        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: লঙ্ঘন করা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "লঙ্ঘন করা — lôngghôn kôrā — \"to violate; to break (a law, an agreement)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কোম্পানিটা চুক্তি লঙ্ঘন করল। kompāniṭā chukti lôngghôn kôrlô. The company broke the contract."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি নিয়মটা লঙ্ঘন করলেন, tini niyômṭā lôngghôn kôrlen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "লঙ্ঘন করা (lôngghôn kôrā) is Sanskrit laṅghana, leaping over and so overstepping, a violation (Monier-Williams), with করা: to step across the line a law draws."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
